   348	## 12. Canon conflicts found in the source (for owner ruling; drafting proceeds on the recommendation unless the owner rules otherwise)
   349	
   350	- **C1 · The cart, the horse and the purse vanish across the seam.** The edition's Book 6 ends (ch60) with a cart, a brown gelding, three boxes and a case under one canvas, and a pooled purse larger than Cael had expected. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] B7 never mentions the cart or horse. The boxes ride a carter's grain (Ch1); the crew hires the smith's cart (Ch5); by day 49 they have "Eighteen marks earned and about ten left after the jug" and sleep in the meadow. **OWNER #23 (binding):** stage it in M1. The horse is a city animal on mule roads (fodder, noise, "paper" written on it), and the cart is too wide for the scrub ruts past Lowmarch. They are sold in Lowmarch's first week. The sale and what remains of the Book 6 purse become a sealed **reserve** that the crew agrees not to live on (Brom's rule: we eat what the board pays). The log's "in hand" counts only the board purse, so every figure in the prose and in Book 8 stands. This is no longer pending. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N7]
   351	- **C2 · The crew's mule.** From Ch16–17 the crew has "a mule" while Oryn has gone north "with … the mule's spare rope in her hand for the next hold's beast." At Millrace there are two mules; at the fork Oryn takes one and the crew keeps one, which stays in the ferryman's shed through the cold term (Book 8). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; unlisted named-season hit found by the item-16 grep, same substitution as line 40] **Recommend:** stage Oryn's decision at Thornwater (day 110–111). She leaves her own mule with the crew for the boxes and a one-armed girl, and takes the route's beast at Millrace. An Oryn decision beat; no prose fact changes.
   352	- **C3 · Karis's measurements.** Ch23: "I've paced two and cord-measured the third." The Stair's perimeter was never paced on the page (Ch18: "I'll pace it in the morning", and the morning was the trap). At the Hall she stood "with the cord in her hand and not laid" (Ch21). **Recommend:** stage the Stair pacing on the morning of day 115 under Teague's rim watch, and the Hall's cord laid during the two marsh days (119–120). Ch23's sentence and the bible's "same radius at the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall" then become true on the page.
   353	- **C4 · "An index of forty-one kinds."** The universe bible and the canon ledger describe the kit's field ledger as carrying "an index of forty-one kinds." In the prose the ledger carries a *site designation in an index Seln does not know*, and forty-one is **Karis's count of kinds of carved line**, the same at the Ring and the Stair (Ch20; Book 8 Ch11 agrees). **Follow the prose.** Flag the bible wording for the canon pass.
   354	- **C5 · Brom's title.** Ch3: Brom answering teeth "for three years and a Copper Crown." The Copper Crown was Lira's (B4). Brom's is the continental Copper title (B5/B6; edition B6 ch55–57's "continental Copper title") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit C1; item-16 hit, retargeted by the item 13 standings rule]. **Render as his continental title.**
   355	- **C6 · Oryn's lateness and the letter.** Ch12's "The route's eleven days north of here" and Ch15's "nine days late here and eleven at the next" do not reconcile (seams F5a, accepted as spoken). Ch18 projects Thornwater "eleven days late"; the closed prose then says **three weeks** at the fork (Ch23) and in the letter (Ch24), and Book 8 Ch1 quotes "Nobody died of three weeks." The architecture card and `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` still say "eleven days." **The edition protects "three weeks."** Recommend writing Ch12's figure as a distance ("the far end of the route is eleven days north of here") and keeping the lateness arithmetic honest from day 104 (nine and eleven) to day 110 (Oxhollow seventeen) to the fork (three weeks).
   356	- **C7 · Oryn's age.** "Late twenties" (Ch6, Cael's catalogue) against "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something…" (Ch13). With Kindling LOCKED at fourteen, that makes her about twenty-five. **Recommend** never stating her age. "Late twenties" stays Cael's estimate; "eleven years" stands.
   357	- **C8 · The Tide stall.** The bible (PROVISIONAL) defines a combat stall that Oryn "has done three times in her life." Neither Book 7 nor Book 8 shows it. **Recommend:** at most one mention, in Oryn's teaching in M3 as a limit she names and hates. Never used, since she is never made to fight. Owner may prefer omission.
   358	- **C9 · Lira's ankle.** The architecture checkpoint says the ankle was "mended once (Ch6)." The prose mended the tibia; the ankle is never mended in Book 7 ("a tape and a season"), and Book 8 Ch1 mends it. **Prose governs.**
   359	- **C10 · The tenth inside a line.** The bible says "all ten fragments function inside." Book 7 shows nine working inside the Ring (the tenth was not yet held). The tenth is never used inside any line in Book 7 ("used on no one" at the Stair and the Hall). **Do not add a Tide test inside a line.** Flag the bible sentence for the canon pass.
   360	- **C11 · Small counts.** Ch17 has Pike turning the ledger "which he had done once before" (it was twice: Ch2, Ch8). Ch24 has "twice in a season" (it is the fourth). Ch22 has "no captain eleven lines up" when Teague is ten up at eleventh. The retelling counts honestly. Convention: "N up" counts positions above; "N between" counts lines between.
   361	- **Already resolved in the prose (do not reopen):** the Lowmarch–Thornwater road is two days; the rib clock (tape off on the 99th at "twenty-one days"); cash 116 → 108 → 102 → 96; Ch23 at the fork is four people and one mule; the sling is "five weeks"; Millrace (EXC-B7-003); the arrested stake (EXC-B7-004); the outer-coping trials (EXC-B7-005); "Twelve weeks" (EXC-B7-001); "two weeks old" (EXC-B7-002); Lira holds Oryn's crossbow from the Hall, not the fork.
   362	- **Already ruled elsewhere and followed here:** Bracken is *he* (OWNER-DECISIONS #7). Vastin's "forty years" is his own rounding, with no age stated (Book 8 ruling 20; OWNER-DECISIONS #8). The narration uses "the academy above Ostrand" (Book 8 decision 9). Registry collisions are not renamed in this edition.
