   348	## AFTER MOVEMENT 3 — chapters 15–22, days 70–84 past the Line (windows to day 92) (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
   349	
   350	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   351	- **Deployment since the Line stays ONE.** No fragment was used on the mountain: Compression and Anchor wanted, and Cael held. Shadow sealed and unused. Lira's burst on day 78 is her own native Wind; her body went about twenty feet and her DECLARATION, with its crack, crossed the gorge.
   352	- **The herd's sense is DERIVED, not tested** (Karis: the ledge went and the declaration followed in the same breath — two causes in an accident, not one cause in a test). Derived on the 75th, used on the 78th. The animals are never given a Path. The herd's dead are "heard, not sworn"; twenty-five were counted on the 81st and the missing five are not entered as dead.
   353	- **Karis's lattice:** nine points and eight channels on the mountain, no join longer than eight paces (Drawn Channel's canon limit; a channel holds only while both points hold; her maximum is sixteen points). Her farthest point is not capped. It empties her.
   354	- **Oryn** is the first healer met past the Line. Tide as taught: contact only; about three serious mendings a day fed and slept, two on a road; cannot heal herself; "Because I cannot mend what I can't read."; the short reading (seconds) and the long one (both hands, all of her, minutes) — healing houses say surface and deep. The stall is named once. She knows NOTHING of fragments, has run no deep reading, records nothing and remembers. Her reading of Cael stopped at five; she said only "a river in the dark" and that it has no side she can find. "More than one" is NOT said (Movement 5).
   355	- **The deep-reading plant stands:** four companions know what "both hands, and all of me… minutes" describes; nobody says it; Oryn does not see it.
   356	- **Teague** learned nothing he could not read off a yard. Oryn told him only that she was late; he does not connect his lost day (waiting at a hold for the healer, for his bow's hip) to the five. Pike struck the ford off his hold; that cost him nothing because he chose the pass.
   357	- **Bodies** [corrected at close, 2026-10-11: an earlier version of this bullet wrongly said Cael's calf was mended; "the leg" the packet means is LIRA'S]: **Lira's right tibia, broken on the 78th, was set and MENDED by Oryn on the 80th** (straight and new; to walk within the week; not to be run on for a month). **Lira's right ANKLE is NOT mended** ("a tape and a season"); her right boot is under the plate and she is barefoot on that side, taped, through day 84. **Cael:** three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break (whole on the 99th by Oryn's rule). **His calf (the ford bite) is NOT mended by anyone: it is cloth-bound and healing on its own.** Karis emptied by the lattice. Exact states in the author's section below, as corrected after repair.
   358	- **Objects:** the hired cart and its load are lost (the ferryman's rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, flour); the smith's six is the only priced debt and the rope's replacement is open and unpriced. The three boxes are recovered; Brom's hedging bill and his older ash wedge survive. Cael's coat has lost both sleeves.
   359	- **Seln** went down for help at first light on the 80th; Oryn had already started up because a carter said they were late.
   360	- **Withheld and intact:** nobody mentions quiet ground; of Oryn's seven holds only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named; no new names; "nineteen" does not appear.
