   390	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   391	**Calendar.** Dusk on the **eighty-fourth day past the Line**, on Oxhollow's bank. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term" twice; "frost"; "the next dry spell"). Days on the page: 70, 71, 72, 73, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 82, 83 (in passing), 84; and, in Oryn's window only, 86, 89, 91 and 92. Weather: dry roads; first ice on a kettle on the 74th and frost on the bench each morning after; a cold rain on the 79th; milder in the valley. The next movement opens on Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th, or the morning after.
   392	
   393	**Where everyone is.** The five are at Oxhollow, in the yard and at the ford, with three boxes on the ground against the gate-house wall. Oryn has gone north out of the gate at dusk with her mule, and is due at Thornwater on the 93rd. Teague and his three have crossed the ford southward at dusk with two mules, a day ahead of the five on the Lowmarch road.
   394	
   395	**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
   396	
   397	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went; none refused more hardly than the second. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word. She asked for the ankle once.
   398	
   399	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; the Skin did not start under the cart at the eighth narrowing. **Left forearm opened at the wrist on the 78th (two boxes), mended on the 80th; in a linen cuff; a week from the middle of the 80th, to take what sits on it and nothing that hangs from it.** He carried the third box down the mountain on his back. He has the hedging bill.
   400	
   401	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **One declaration on the 78th: nine points and eight channels, held eight seconds. Empty since;** told to ask nothing of herself for a week from the 80th. She could not strike a flint on the 78th, wrote one line on the 82nd and held the purse on the 84th. Holds: the long leaf's fair copy is with Oxhollow's keeper (see below); the derived page (shale-backs), in her hand, with the ford finding beside it in Lira's; everything in the three boxes; the carter's map. She has met a primary source who keeps no book, and has asked her nothing she was not invited to.
   402	
   403	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. No Path lifted. Unmarked. He found every sleeping place, noted the pale rock, crossed the live slide for water, walked the lip twice and marked forty-four stones, and went down for help on the 80th. He lent Karis his coat from the 78th. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.** He gave reports unasked on the 72nd, the 75th and the 79th, since each bore.
   404	
   405	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken", and has put one day on her route for it (her window, the 92nd). She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record.
   406	
   407	**Teague.** At Oxhollow's ford at dusk on the 84th he said his four things and crossed. He knows: no cart; a leg and a wrist mended by the route's healer; the girl's foot strapped; the small one asleep sitting up; the boy's ribs taped; that the mountain came down and all five came off it; that the keeper paid seventy for a no. He does not know what Cael is. He and his three (the spear, the bow, the boy) and two mules are a day ahead on the road south.
   408	
   409	**Objects and money.** **The cart is in the gorge**, with the ferryman's rope, the blankets, the kettle, the canvas and the flour. Three boxes, whole; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. Seln's case. Hesk's satchel, with the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and Pike's lines on bark. Karis's lantern, cord, brass straightedge and Hesk's clock. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two marks earned** (62 + Oxhollow 70); **a hundred and sixteen in hand**; **six owed to the smith** for the cart. Pike's slip is in hand, with five strokes and Oxhollow's mark at its foot, to be carried to the plank. The long leaf was unrolled on the keeper's board and paid for there; the text does not say who carries it away, and the keeper is its buyer.
   410	
   411	**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged since the 69th: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up. The traverse is not yet said.
   412	
   413	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Oryn knows that a healer's hands cannot read him and that he heals fast; she has been told nothing. Oxhollow's keeper knows that a Path used under the shale-backs brings the hill down, as derived. **Nobody has mentioned quiet ground.** Oryn's other holds are unnamed; Thornwater and Oxhollow are the only two named.
   414	
   415	**Open threads.** A fourth reading, at Thornwater, in nine days, and what four of the five felt when a healer said "both hands, and all of me". Twenty-one days of tape. Karis's reserve. A leg that may not run for a month and an ankle that will set. Six marks owed for a cart, and a rope. What Pike will write for a job that delivered a no and lost a cart. "The same contract inside a season." Five animals fewer on a hill, heard and not sworn. Two hounds still open below Thornwater's ford. Lira's question, now with a job in it and a ledge under it. Hesk's letter, and no roof.
