editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:436:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:437:- **The line (OWNER-pending #49, default in force).** At the line the five live Arbiters stop at the same step: Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's. Cael's own Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling and nothing in him changes there; his fragments go on answering inside. The protected log entries are word for word (their loose "mine" is his shorthand). Outside them nothing says "his Path", nothing says his Arbiter is awake or unaffected, and nothing says WHY the fragments answer. The word *Quieting* has not been said. "Compact" has not been said aloud: the stake carries the registry stamp. "Made" has been said of the place once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:439:- **Ring geometry — the manuscript governs (Movement 5 inherits):** the western line stone is 220 yards from the floor's middle; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is under the floor's EASTERN lip; so den to the western line is about 233 yards and den to the eastern perimeter about 207. The protected round is 1,374 yards and a piece (sixty-two cords and twenty strides); radius ten cords; the constant offset is six and a half feet per cord. NO cord length and NO stride length is stated, and none is to be added. "A hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:441:- **The trials at the line** ran Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn. Lira's full burst became one step; her words on stepping back out are the protected clock line. Oryn has crossed twice (with Brom; with the six) and reads nobody inside; her eight solo crossings are Movement 5's. Seln's map memory is Movement 5's.
