   470	- **The Ring's ground (flag; one picture for chapters 27–30):** at the crest of a long rise the ruts swing out to the north and come back to their line on the far side, keeping about forty yards from the line all the way round. The line crosses the old straight line of the road **eighty of Cael's strides** beyond the turn; Karis's grey stone marks it (the circle's western point). The camp is at the turn. The floor is three hundred yards from the turn. The perimeter is walked from the stone northward, with the ring on the right hand; Brom cuts a turf at each cord; the constant offset is **six feet and a half** to the cord.
