   242	**Documents, slips and notices**
   243	- Pike's Thornwater-road line (Ch1): *Thornwater road, the stretch. Walked ahead of one cart, one carter, one mule. Delivered at the fence. No losses. Nine marks, paid.*
   244	- Pike's ford line (Ch3–4): *Stillhound pack, Thornwater ford: cleared. Five confirmed. Crew of five, four injured, none lost. Price paid.*
   245	- Pike's traverse line (Ch8): "High traverse, Oxhollow to Thornwater. Mapped. Delivered at the ford. Carts go round." … "Cart lost. Crew of five, three hurt, none lost. Seventy." … *less six, the cart.* — "Seventy's what the ford paid. Sixty-four's what the job was worth. That's what goes on the wall."
   246	- The Fallow slip (Ch8, Ch12): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Fallow road. East of Thornwater; the second day; where the road leaves its line at the rise and comes back to it. One hundred marks (one hundred).* Seal: a hook and a bar, in dark wax.
   247	- Pike's Fallow copy (Ch14; read again Ch17): *Recovery, Fallow road, broker's posting. Taken. Witnessed. Completed: incomplete — instruments not recovered — crew returned. Six went in. Six came out. No price paid.*
   248	- The Stair slip (Ch17): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Stair road. South of Lowmarch; the first day; where the road drops off the ridge and the ground opens. Three hundred marks (three hundred).*
