+# Movement 005 source-distance tracking
+
+Independent side-by-side read of source chapters 11–13 against manuscript chapters 31–37. Protected units, wording quoted in `MOVEMENT-005.md`, and facts or event sequences required by the packet, `BOOK_MAP.md`, or `STATE_LEDGER.md` were excluded wherever the manuscript supplied a genuinely new telling.
+
+The requested pair-output probe was run. Its movement total (4% skeleton / 20% close) is not a count of genuine tracking. In particular, chapter 36 scene 4's 57% skeleton result is the protected covenant, and the exact or near-exact probe pairs in chapters 33–37 are overwhelmingly protected orders, log entries, the covenant, the notice, or packet-quoted exchanges. The independent overlap check also reports **0 unprotected shared runs of 8+ words** and 31 protected runs. The findings below are subtler sentence-content and beat-order matches.
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Ten genuine tracked passages.** Chapter 34 scene 3 is densely tracked, with three passages in one scene. Every other affected scene contains one isolated passage, and every other scene contains none.
+
+| Manuscript chapter | Scene 1 | Scene 2 | Scene 3 | Scene 4 | Scene 5 | Scene 6 | Scene 7 | Chapter total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 31 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | — | — | **1** |
+| 32 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 | — | — | **2** |
+| 33 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | — | — | **1** |
+| 34 | 0 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 0 | — | — | **3** |
+| 35 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | **1** |
+| 36 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | — | — | **1** |
+| 37 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | — | — | **1** |
+| **Movement total** |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | **10** |
+
+Scene numbers follow the manuscript's `---` divisions and the sweep probe. Line ranges are: chapter 31, 1–84 / 86–138 / 140–198 / 200–286 / 288–323; chapter 32, 1–72 / 74–144 / 146–192 / 194–258 / 260–317; chapter 33, 1–56 / 58–128 / 130–184 / 186–240 / 242–279; chapter 34, 1–48 / 50–110 / 112–176 / 178–204 / 206–309; chapter 35, 1–60 / 62–116 / 118–152 / 154–216 / 218–262 / 264–302 / 304–375; chapter 36, 1–40 / 42–116 / 118–198 / 200–228 / 230–277; chapter 37, 1–40 / 42–98 / 100–144 / 146–203 / 205–246.
+
+## Tracked passages
+
+| chapter:line | Manuscript opening words | Source sentence followed | Kind | Beat chain to break without opening the source |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 31:295 | “She took her hands away as though the arm had burnt them.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-11.md:69` — “She said nothing else. She had the linen out…” | split | The packet requires failed hands, cloth and knees, and the command to move; those elements are excluded. The extra procedure still follows the source sentence's order: linen appears immediately after the failed read, a knee loads the arm above the elbow, pressure is maintained while the wrapping advances, and the work ends in a hard knot. Start with Karis already holding pressure and make Oryn improvise the binding from a garment, or have Oryn give verbal steps while somebody else performs them in a different order. |
+| 32:129 | “He had its weight. He had been carrying a pace and a half…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-11.md:119` — “He got the hound by the loose skin at the back of its neck…” | varied | “The throw” is required; its mechanics are not. Both tellings take the hound behind the skull and at the hind end, remove its rear purchase, turn the throw through Cael's back or hip, make the jaws release because the animal cannot brace, and land it in the south grass. Break the chain by using the lane edge, another person's leverage, or the animal's forward motion; do not begin with the neck-and-hindquarter grip. |
+| 32:247 | “He had priced this count too, and the price was a bad one.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-11.md:149` — “The second burst was the turn, west…” | split | The second Wind lock and Compression at contact are required. Beyond that, both passages isolate one hound inside the lock, leave Cael unable to move, put his upper body between himself and the strike, bring Compression in late, conduct the force through shoulder, spine and legs into the ground, and throw the animal sideways before Cael runs west. Let the hound hit from behind or low at the calf, or let the late Compression collapse Cael with the animal rather than turning him briefly into a standing wall. |
+| 33:59 | “He held the lantern for an hour, and for the whole of it he watched her face.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-11.md:201` — “He watched it, because he could not have stood up to go elsewhere.” | varied | The hour and lantern are required. The added observation follows the source's private sequence: Cael watches the healer rather than the arm, remembers her visibly aging over the mountain mending, then measures the present cost through sweat in the cold and the colour draining or bruising under her eyes. Enter through Lira's changing grip or the lantern's oil; let another character notice Oryn's cost only after the hour is over. |
+| 34:121 | “She took Karis first. Two fingers went to the inside of a thin wrist…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-12.md:51` — “Both hands, either side of Karis's throat…” | split | Karis's throat mending and its required spoken outcome are excluded. The procedure keeps the source progression: contact at throat and jaw, a count to ten, still treatment, the trapped swallow releasing, and the bruise changing by roughly a week's colour while the healer pays for it. Begin after the treatment with Karis testing water or breath, or make the first visible change her voice attempting and failing rather than bruise colour and swallowing. |
+| 34:137 | “It was quicker than the throat. When she let go of him…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-12.md:69` — “Shorter than the throat; less than half, by the floor.” | near-verbatim | Both sentences explicitly compare the hand's duration with the throat's, reveal pale or dark lines where the open cuts were when Oryn releases him, and have Brom close then reopen the healed hand or fists. The protected “String… That's two” unit is not part of this finding. Give the result through function first—Brom picking up a cup, failing a fine movement, or flexing at Oryn's order—and describe the remaining marks later, if at all. |
+| 34:149 | “He had not expected it. He had thought that she would take her two hours first…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-12.md:81` — “He got the trouser leg up, and the cloth with it…” | split | The fourth failed read and protected finding are required. The surrounding procedure preserves the source order: old binding comes off, the wound is washed, Oryn brackets it above and below, the count stops without finding Cael, she repeats the established rule, notices the cut closing by itself, and rebinds it instead of mending. Reverse the diagnostic route: have her name the visible spontaneous closure before touching him, then try the read only because Lira challenges the visual finding; end on refusal to spend more linen rather than another completed binding. |
+| 35:283 | “They came down to the fork an hour after noon…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-13.md:5` — “The wall, timber on a stone footing, the same.” | varied | The arrival at Thornwater, flat-footed walk, and packet-quoted “Six. Well.” are excluded. The extra staging still makes the steading's woman meet them at the gate, count them one head at a time, inventory the sling, throat, hands or rags, Cael's body, healer and mule, and only then deliver the protected count. Open inside the yard with the broth already waiting, or let the bowman or a child spot one changed body first and make the woman's count arrive later, without a head-to-injury inventory. |
+| 36:3 | “There was a finger of oil in Karis's lantern…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-13.md:35` — “The loft, after the meal, the five of them and the lantern…” | split | The loft council is required, but this opening retains the source tableau: the measured lantern oil first, then Lira against grain with the sling, Brom stationed by the ladder with marked hands open, Karis with notebook and damaged throat, and Seln placed to monitor the yard, in that order. Enter on Cael drawing up the ladder or on Karis tearing out the later leaf; distribute the others' positions only when each speaks, in a different order, rather than inventorying all four before the council begins. |
+| 37:21 | “It did not go down. It went along.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-13.md:157` — “It came in under the front hand first.” | varied | The packet's “along, not down” direction and the fact that Cael can feel Oryn keeping time are excluded. The added sensation chain still follows the source: the current becomes water moving through a channel, travels his length, resolves into a regular pace identified as Oryn's road gait, and thereby turns an impersonal reading into the felt presence of a person who keeps time. Keep the direction and timing facts, but use a non-water image and identify her through an irregularity in pressure, breath, or hand placement before any cadence is recognized. |
+
+## Densely tracked scene
+
+### Chapter 34, scene 3 (lines 112–176)
+
+Re-enter after Karis's treatment, with her already drinking and testing the swallow while Oryn states only the required voice prognosis. Give Brom's result through a practical action—he tries to fasten the crossbow sleeve or lift the pan—and defer any description of the healed lines. When Oryn turns to Cael, let her inspect and name the visibly half-closed seam before she touches him; Lira's challenge can then force the failed read, after which Oryn leaves the old or Karis-made binding in place rather than repeating the source's wash–bracket–fail–rebind progression. This preserves throat, hand, calf, the protected finding, and the morning arithmetic while replacing all three source-shaped treatment procedures.
+
+No other scene needs wholesale rerouting. Its single finding can be broken locally using the final column above.

